 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Construction involves Morton ordering and bucketing, which is generally $O(N \log N)$ or $O(N)$ depending on implementation, followed by bottom-up aggregation [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The structure reduces memory footprint by factoring multiple primitives into single equivalent planks at coarser levels, allowing the model to fit within hardware budgets [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Designed for real-time rendering on consumer GPUs, serving varying budgets (render farm, desktop, laptop, VR headset) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Enables real-time large-scale rendering by dynamically selecting the appropriate level of detail based on view-dependent footprint and available memory [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires a frozen trained model; the factoring process introduces approximation error, though bounded by the union-volume estimates and adaptive-approximation rates [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** When deploying large-scale Gaussian Splatting models on hardware with strict memory constraints and requiring real-time performance [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** When exact geometric fidelity is required without any approximation, or when the model is not trained/frozen [S1, unofficial].
